{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fixed deterministic xdist skip-summary coverage in worktree `.rebar/worktrees/fix-985f-xdist-skip`, commit `be60dc6349a0eecfc1d97e50b8433de9248ea6b2`.\n\nEvidence:\n- Ambient-probe reproduction with fake working `ps`: inner pytest reported `2 passed`, outer assertion failed expecting `skipped=2`.\n- Ambient-probe unavailable path: target passed when `ps` was unavailable to the inner run.\n- Fixed test with fake working `ps`: target passed.\n- Fixed test with `ps` absent from inner `PATH`: target passed.\n- Hollowing guard: temporarily disabling `collect_counted_skips_from_worker` made the target fail because `sandbox compatibility skips: 4` disappeared, then the aggregation code was restored.\n- Focused related tests: `pytest -q tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_985f.py tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py` => `46 passed, 1 skipped`; the sibling skip is the intentional live adapter assertion for this sandbox.\n- `make verify` ran to completion and remains red only in known pre-existing classes: pandoc/wiki-render (17), doctor (10), sandbox/SemLock (5). `tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_985f.py::test_sandbox_skip_summary_aggregates_across_xdist_workers` is no longer in the failure list."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789746165016260142,"uuid":"708dee99-b304-4e48-90b7-93eb7f55022c"}